    "summary": "Cloth (aso oke woman&#039;s wrapper) composed of 14 hand-woven strips of imported cotton, machine sewn together and machine hemmed. The cloth is composed of two types of narrow strip arranged to form two bands in the manner of Yoruba woman&#039;s weave:\r\n1. light and dark blue warps and blue wefts. There are also rows of punched holes.\r\n2.  warp stripes in magenta, green, black and yellow, with black wefts. This too has rows of punched holes.   The cloth is machine hemmed.",
